{title: Whom Shall I Fear}
{subtitle: Psalms 27:1–5}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 128}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | ×17

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
When the wicked close around me [C#]and they come to tear [D#m]me down
They are the ones who stumble [C#]and they crash onto [D#m]the ground
Let an army camp against me, let [C#]the war break out to[D#m]night
Even then I will be confident, the [C#]LORD is my light
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The [D#m]LORD is my [F#]light and my sal[C#]vation
Whom shall I [D#m]fear?
[F#]The LORD [C#]is the stronghold of my life
Of whom shall [B]I be af[D#m]raid?
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
One thing I ask of the LORD, [C#]this is what I [D#m]seek
To dwell in the house of the LORD all [C#]the days of my [D#m]life
To gaze on the beauty of the LORD
[C#]And to seek him in his temple
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[B]The LORD is my light and my [D#m]salvation
Whom [F#]shall I fear?
The LORD [C#]is the stronghold of my [D#m]life
Of whom [F#]shall I be af[C#]raid?
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
In the day of trouble he will keep me [B]safe in his shel[D#m]ter [F#][C#][D#m][F#][C#]
He will [D#m]hide me under [F#]the cover of [C#]his tent
And set me high [D#m]upon a [F#]rock
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The LORD is [C#]my light and my salvation
Whom shall I fear?
[B]The LORD is the [D#m]stronghold of my life
Of [F#]whom shall I be af[D#m]raid?
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F#]Wait for the [C#]light
Be strong, and let your heart [D#m]take [F#]courage
Wait [C#]for the light
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
